    "title": "Chessboard Game",
    "category": "Mathematics - Game Theory",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "A token is placed on an N \u00d7 N chessboard at position (x, y). On each turn, a player may move the token only to one of the allowed positions defined by the game's movement rules. A player who cannot make a move loses. Determine whether the starting player has a winning strategy.",
    "input": "Integer N Starting coordinates (x, y)",
    "output": "Print \"First\" if the starting player wins; otherwise, print \"Second\".",
    "constraints": "1 <= N <= 200 1 <= x, y <= N"
